Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:00:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PM P3: zero-duration S1 and close-out (PM_PLAN P3, complete)

The S1 fork measured in P2 (PM_PLAN 2c: no consumer needs
real device parking; an instantly-pending wake event is
spec-legal) lands as zero-duration S1: the SLP_TYP=1 write
latches WAK_STS, the event flows through the normal SCI
expression if enabled, and the run continues -- a guest's
resume path exercises exactly what it must on any
fast-waking machine, deterministically and snapshot-safe.
The DSDT grows the matching \_S1 = Package(1,0) next to
\_S5, both pinned byte-for-byte to the decoder. Unknown
sleep types still log and do nothing.

NC: pm.c+acpi.c at P2 -- both suites abort (WAK_STS;
DSDT length). Gates: make test + sanitize green, both
SeaBIOS ISO lanes green with the stock BIOS. PM_PLAN is
complete; stated limits (no GPE sources, no S3/S4, S1
never parks, no SMM) are recorded in the plan close-out.
Docs: PM_PLAN.md (P3 receipts, D5 resolved, COMPLETE),
ROADMAP.md (candidate #3 closed), STATUS.md, CHANGELOG.md.
